# cli-rust

This package demonstrates how **arb** can generate a real Rust CLI using
[clap](https://github.com/clap-rs/clap).

It is intentionally small but non-trivial, and shows:

- global flags
- leaf commands
- nested subcommands (`remote add`, `remote list`)
- correct help output at every level

All CLI structure is defined in data, not handwritten Rust.

## How it works

- `schema.yaml` defines the allowed CLI shape
- `examples/data.nested.yaml` describes a CLI with nested subcommands
- `templates/` contains the code templates used to generate the CLI

Running `arb compile` produces a fully working Rust CLI project.

## Try it

From the repo root:

```cmd
arb compile --package packages/cli-rust ^
  --data packages/cli-rust/examples/data.nested.yaml ^
  --out out

cd out
cargo run -- --help
cargo run -- status --help
cargo run -- remote add foo https://example.com
```

## Why this exists

This example exists to show that arb can generate **real, idiomatic CLIs**
without hand-written glue code, while keeping validation and determinism.

It is meant as a learning and reference package.